From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 10:39:54 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali: allow non-secure ADSP FastRPC
 sessions

Mark the ADSP FastRPC node as a non-secure domain, as on SM8650, so the
fastrpc driver also creates /dev/fastrpc-adsp. Userspace such as
hexagonrpcd needs it to start the sensors protection domain on the ADSP;
without it only /dev/fastrpc-adsp-secure exists.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
index 9dc5f932abc5..451e9f2ca1d0 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
@@ -3452,6 +3452,7 @@
 					compatible = "qcom,kaanapali-fastrpc";
 					qcom,glink-channels = "fastrpcglink-apps-dsp";
 					label = "adsp";
+					qcom,non-secure-domain;
 					#address-cells = <1>;
 					#size-cells = <0>;
 
